# Edge Detection in Grayscale Images

## Problem Description
Implement a class `GrayscaleImage` that represents a grayscale image and can perform edge detection using the Sobel operator. The Sobel operator is used in image processing to highlight regions of high spatial frequency that correspond to edges in the image.

## Class Requirements
Your implementation must include the following exactly as specified:

```cpp
class GrayscaleImage {
private:
    vector<vector<int>> pixels;
    int width;
    int height;

public:
    // Constructs a blank image with given dimensions (all pixels initialized to 0)
    GrayscaleImage(int w, int h);

    // Constructs an image from existing pixel data (throws invalid_argument if empty)
    GrayscaleImage(const vector<vector<int>>& pixel_data);

    // Returns the width of the image
    int get_width() const;

    // Returns the height of the image
    int get_height() const;

    // Returns the pixel value at (y, x)
    int get_pixel(int y, int x) const;

    // Sets the pixel value at (y, x)
    void set_pixel(int y, int x, int value);

    // Applies Sobel operator for edge detection (modifies the image in-place)
    void detect_edges();

    // Prints the image matrix (for debugging purposes)
    void print_image() const;
};
```

## Implementation Notes
1. The Sobel operator uses two 3x3 kernels (one for horizontal and one for vertical changes) to approximate the gradient at each pixel.
2. The gradient magnitude should be calculated as sqrt(gx² + gy²) and clamped to 255.
3. Edge detection should only be applied to interior pixels (those not on the image border).
4. Pixel values should be in the range 0-255 (no need to validate input values).

## Constraints
- Image dimensions will be at least 1x1
- All pixel values will be between 0 and 255 (inclusive)
- Coordinates passed to get_pixel/set_pixel will always be valid

## Example Usage
```cpp
// Create a 3x3 image with a vertical edge
vector<vector<int>> image_data = {
    {100, 100, 0},
    {100, 100, 0},
    {100, 100, 0}
};

GrayscaleImage img(image_data);
img.detect_edges();

// After edge detection, the center pixel should show the edge
cout << "Edge strength at center: " << img.get_pixel(1, 1) << endl;
// Expected output: Edge strength at center: 255
```

## Testing
Your implementation will be tested with various images including:
- Simple edges (vertical, horizontal, diagonal)
- Uniform images (no edges)
- Small and large images
- Edge cases (1x1 images)

The test cases will verify that:
1. Edge detection correctly identifies edges
2. Non-edge areas remain unchanged
3. Image borders are not modified
4. The image dimensions are correctly maintained
5. Pixel access methods work correctly

## Submission Requirements
Submit a single C++ file containing your complete `GrayscaleImage` class implementation. Do not include the test functions in your submission.

