```

## Constraints
- All calculations must use double precision floating point
- Motor must be enabled before any movement occurs
- Position/speed updates must follow proper acceleration/deceleration profiles
- For targeted movements, the motor should automatically calculate when to start decelerating

## Notes
- Your implementation must exactly match the class specification above
- The motor parameters (stepsPerRev, microSteps, gearRatio) affect how physical steps translate to revolutions
- Position values can be positive or negative (representing direction)
- Speed values can be positive or negative (positive = forward, negative = backward)

