# Steering Behaviors Implementation

## Problem Description
Implement a system for managing steering behaviors in a 2D space. The system should include a vector class for 2D operations, a blackboard for shared data storage, and two specific steering behaviors (Seek and Flee) that inherit from a base steering behavior class.

## Class Requirements

### Vector2 Class
Implement a 2D vector class with the following specifications:
```cpp
class Vector2 {
public:
    float x, y;

    Vector2(float x = 0.0f, float y = 0.0f);
    Vector2 operator+(const Vector2& other) const;
    Vector2 operator-(const Vector2& other) const;
    Vector2 operator*(float scalar) const;
    float magnitude() const;
    Vector2 normalized() const;
    static float distance(const Vector2& a, const Vector2& b);
};
```

### Blackboard Class
Implement a blackboard class for storing and retrieving different types of data:
```cpp
class Blackboard {
private:
    std::unordered_map<std::string, float> floatValues;
