public:
    FleeBehavior(const Vector2& threatPos = Vector2(), float distance = 10.0f);
    Vector2 update() override;
    void setThreat(const Vector2& newThreat);
    std::string getName() const override;
};
```

## Example Usage
```cpp
int main() {
    // Create a blackboard and set initial values
    Blackboard bb;
    bb.setVector("position", Vector2(0, 0));
    bb.setVector("velocity", Vector2(0, 0));
    bb.setFloat("max_speed", 5.0f);

    // Create and configure seek behavior
    SeekBehavior seek(Vector2(10, 0));
    seek.initialise(&bb);
    seek.setWeight(1.0f);

    // Get steering force from seek behavior
    Vector2 steeringForce = seek.update();
    std::cout << "Steering force: (" << steeringForce.x << ", " << steeringForce.y << ")" << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

## Constraints
1. All classes must be implemented exactly as specified
2. The Vector2 class must provide all specified mathematical operations
3. Steering behaviors must properly use the blackboard for shared data
4. The system should handle disabled behaviors appropriately
5. All floating-point comparisons should account for minor precision differences

## Evaluation Criteria
1. Correct implementation of all specified classes and methods
2. Proper handling of vector mathematics
3. Correct behavior of seek and flee algorithms
4. Proper use of the blackboard system
5. Handling of edge cases (disabled behaviors, zero vectors, etc.)

