# RPG Equipment and Enchantment System

## Problem Description
You are tasked with implementing a class hierarchy for an RPG game's equipment and enchantment system. The system should model different types of equipment (weapons and armor) that can be enhanced with magical enchantments. Each piece of equipment has basic properties and can be enchanted with various magical effects that modify its value and behavior.

## Class Requirements

### Enchant Class (Abstract Base Class)
```cpp
class Enchant {
public:
    Enchant(string name, int power, string effect);
    virtual ~Enchant();

    string getName() const;
    int getPower() const;
    string getEffect() const;

    virtual void applyEffect() = 0;

protected:
    string m_name;
    int m_power;
    string m_effect;
};
```

### Equipment Class (Abstract Base Class)
```cpp
class Equipment {
public:
    Equipment(string name, int wgt, int con);
    virtual ~Equipment();

    string getName() const;
    int getWeight() const;
    int getCondition() const;
    int getMaxCondition() const;
    bool isEnchanted() const;

    void setCondition(int con);
